<title>ESTONIA: C.BANK CONFIRMS WAS IN TALKS WITH SWEDBANK.</title>
<headline>C.BANK CONFIRMS WAS IN TALKS WITH SWEDBANK.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's central bank confirmed on Wednesday that it has been in talks with Swedbank to sell its stake in Hoiupank, adding that no decisions have been made yet.</p>
<p>&quot;There have been negotiations, but no concrete decisions have been made,&quot; Kaja Kell, the deputy head of the central bank's press department, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Kell added that the central bank will make a statement on the issue later today.</p>
<p>Hoiupank earlier announced that Swedbank might buy the central bank's stake in it, which would increase the Swedish bank's stake from 12.5 percent to 25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
